# L2-SYN-018: four polls of one message with an unchanging payload, 100 us
# apart. Every byte matches between the four records except the IRIG
# timestamp's lower word (21F6, 85F6, E9F6, 4DF7). This is an ordinary
# periodic transaction, so it SHALL decode -- through 5.2.0 the
# homogeneous-payload check ignored the timestamp and rejected the file as
# padding (exit 2). The `homogeneous-payload` case keeps the rejection for
# real fill, whose timestamp bytes repeat along with everything else.
#
# Each record is the 72-byte RT15 SA11 Receive of `count-one.hex`.
